<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clĕon</span></b> , ōnis, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κλέων</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a Grecian proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An Athenian popular leader</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep.
				4, 10, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Brut. 7,
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A rhetorician of Halicarnassus</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Lys. 3,
			5</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A statuary</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 8,
				19, § 37</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A painter</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				11, 40, § 140</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
